<DocsLayout title="Haft v9 skills, CLI, and MCP" description="Reference for the 12 independent skills, current CLI families, 12 MCP tools, and removed execution surfaces.">
  <h1>Skills, CLI &amp; MCP</h1>

  <p>
    Haft exposes one project graph through host-agent skills, a manual CLI, and
    the <code>haft serve</code> MCP server. The surfaces share the same kernel
    contracts, but they do not carry the same authority. A visible command or
    schema is not permission to perform its effect.
  </p>

  <h2>The 12 v9 skills</h2>

  <p>
    These are independent capabilities, not workflow stages. Auto means the
    host may route a matching request to the skill. It does not mean the skill
    may invent operator authority or persist every result.
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Skill</th>
        <th>Routing</th>
        <th>Current condition</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>h-reason</code></td><td>auto</td><td>Ambiguous FPF-aware question that needs the source-first umbrella</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>h-frame</code></td><td>auto</td><td>The problem itself is under-articulated</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>h-diagnose</code></td><td>auto</td><td>A concrete failure has rival causes</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>h-explore</code></td><td>auto</td><td>Genuinely distinct candidate approaches are needed</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>h-compare</code></td><td>auto</td><td>Existing candidates need a parity-based comparison</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>h-decide</code></td><td>auto router</td><td>A direct, unambiguous operator request binds one bounded choice</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>h-verify</code></td><td>auto</td><td>A recorded decision or claim must be tested against current evidence</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>h-status</code></td><td>auto</td><td>Live project state, drift, coverage, or readiness is the question</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>h-onboard</code></td><td>auto</td><td>Haft setup or the project profile is absent or incomplete</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>h-spec</code></td><td>auto</td><td>A typed spec carrier, lifecycle act, or source-currentness repair is current</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>h-note</code></td><td>auto</td><td>The operator asks to persist one non-binding fact, observation, caveat, or rationale</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>h-commission</code></td><td>manual only</td><td>The operator grants bounded execution authority through a WorkCommission</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    Completion of one skill never implies that another must follow.
    <code>h-decide</code> can route a sufficiently exact natural-language
    choice; invoking the skill is not itself an approval receipt.
    <code>h-commission</code> remains manual-only.
  </p>

  <h2>Current CLI families</h2>

  <p>Run <code>haft --help</code> for the complete installed command tree.</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>CLI</th>
        <th>Purpose</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>haft init</code></td><td>Initialize project core and selected host integrations</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft serve</code></td><td>Start the project-bound MCP server</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft fpf query|lookup|inspect</code></td><td>Read the source-native FPF publication</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft graph explore</code></td><td>Orient by exact code symbol or bounded concern</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft spec ...</code></td><td>Inspect, validate, review, export, and route typed SpecSection lifecycle actions</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft memory ...</code></td><td>Resolve, read, validate, or admit typed project memory</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft onboard profile ...</code></td><td>Apply one readable, already-prepared profile choice</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft commission ...</code></td><td>Manage runner-neutral WorkCommission records</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft decision ...</code></td><td>Inspect governing sets and decision reconciliation</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft artifact create CAPABILITY --input-file ...</code></td><td>Create or update one artifact through its dedicated effect sink</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft sync</code></td><td>Import git-carried <code>.haft/*.md</code> projections into local SQLite</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft check</code></td><td>Run the deterministic CI-oriented governance check</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft doctor</code></td><td>Inspect installation and project-binding health</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft interface [capability] --json</code></td><td>Read compact machine-readable kernel contracts</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Runtime truth:</strong> use the help and interface output from the
      binary that is actually loaded by the host. Documentation describes the
      release; it cannot prove that a stale MCP process has restarted onto it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>The 12 MCP tools</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Tool</th>
        <th>Purpose</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>haft_note</code></td><td>Persist one non-binding note through the note contract</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft_problem</code></td><td>Frame or characterize a problem</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft_solution</code></td><td>Explore or compare candidate solutions</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft_decision</code></td><td>Decision, claim, evidence, and baseline operations</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft_refresh</code></td><td>Scan and route evidence or decision maintenance</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft_query</code></td><td>Status, FPF, code graph, governing records, specs, and typed-memory reads</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft_method</code></td><td>Pull, close, and recover task-local MethodRuns</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft_commission</code></td><td>Runner-neutral WorkCommission lifecycle</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft_spec_section</code></td><td>Typed SpecSection lifecycle projection and gated acts</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft_onboard</code></td><td>Read setup status and prepare non-binding profile reviews</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft_entity</code></td><td>Establish one minimum non-binding EntityOfConcern with atomic aliases</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>haft_memory</code></td><td>Expert low-level typed-memory validation or admission</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    MCP validates arguments server-side and returns structured errors. Creation
    actions for decisions, commissions, profile changes, and other binding
    effects still require their exact authority path. Model-supplied fields do
    not prove authorization.
  </p>

  <h2>Removed from v9</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><code>haft run</code> and <code>haft harness</code></li>
    <li>the bundled Open-Sleigh and Elixir/OTP/BEAM runtime</li>
    <li><code>/h-search</code>, <code>/h-problems</code>, and <code>/h-view</code></li>
    <li><code>haft fpf search</code>; use <code>query</code>, <code>lookup</code>, or <code>inspect</code></li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Project search, active-problem attention, and projections remain available
    through current <code>haft_query</code> actions and focused CLI families.
    The removed slash-command files are not compatibility aliases.
  </p>

